{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And blessed</b> — the sense of \"the name of His glory\" is the revered Name, which is the proper noun. For there is no name in all languages that is a proper noun except as an epithet, such as HaShem, and also Elohim and Shaddai. Therefore it is written: \"this is My name forever\" (Exodus 3:15), for it alone is one name, and likewise \"and His name is one\" (Zechariah 14:9)." "<b>And the sense of \"may His glory fill\"</b> — His praise." "<b>Amen</b> — from the root of אמונה (faith)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 72, :notes {0 "Resolved ה' as HaShem per voice rules for divine names."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:05.268930005Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}